%[text] # Evaluate Air Cooled Data Center Temperature Profile
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%[text] ## Define Data Center
%[text] This workflow shows how to evaluate an air-cooled data center. The example creates a 500 kW data center with vertical rack air cooling, where the rack assemblies operate under different server load utilizations. The composite library block **Air Cooled PDU Assembly**, from the Simscape custom library, is used for the analysis. Four **Air Cooled PDU Assembly** blocks are parameterized to represent an approximately 500 kW data center, each with four PDU racks and six server trays per PDU rack. The server utilization and fan speed are specified differently for each of the four library blocks. Each block represents one PDU+Fan Assembly unit. Each PDU+Fan Assembly unit contains 36 fans, with the performance curve for each fan provided on the Fans tab of the **Air Cooled PDU Assembly** block mask.
%[text] ![](text:image:9718)
%[text] The data center assets are modeled inside a rectangular room, along with the internal air mass. The **LumpedRoom** subsystem in the **DataCenter** block represents the room. Thermal node *Ts* represents the desired room temperature, *C* represents the cold air entering the server racks, *H* represents the hot air exiting the server racks, and *Amb* represents the ambient heat transfer.
%[text] Specify the room dimensions and the volume occupied by the data center as a percentage of the room volume.
airCooledDataCenter.Room.Length = simscape.Value(40,"m");
airCooledDataCenter.Room.Width  = simscape.Value(30,"m");
airCooledDataCenter.Room.Height = simscape.Value(5,"m");
airCooledDataCenter.Room.RoomAssetVolPercent = 80;
%[text] The **Uvec** subsystem defines the time-varying server utilization for each data center assembly. The **Room HVAC Control** and **Fan Speed Control** subsystems specify the room HVAC and PDU rack fan control, respectively.
%[text] Specify the desired room temperature for data center.
airCooledDataCenter.Room.Tset_K = simscape.Value(291,"K");
%[text] Set the HVAC heat exchanger efficiency percentage.
airCooledDataCenter.Room.HVAC.EffHeatExchanger = 80;
%[text] Set the temperature range over which fan control operates.
airCooledDataCenter.Fan.UpperT = simscape.Value(320,"K");
airCooledDataCenter.Fan.LowerT = simscape.Value(300,"K");
%[text] Specify the ambient temperature, initial component temperatures, and the internal room air heat transfer coefficient values.
airCooledDataCenter.HeatTransfer.AmbientT = simscape.Value(313,"K");
airCooledDataCenter.HeatTransfer.InitialT = simscape.Value(293,"K");
airCooledDataCenter.HeatTransfer.HTC = simscape.Value(50,"W/(K*m^2)");
%[text] This step completes the model setup.
%%
%[text] ## Run Simulation
%[text] %[text:anchor:TMP_5ae1] Open the model for analysis.
airCooledDataCenter.SLXModelName = "AirCooledDataCenterTemperatureProfile";
open_system(airCooledDataCenter.SLXModelName);
%[text] Run model and close.
sim(airCooledDataCenter.SLXModelName);
close_system(airCooledDataCenter.SLXModelName,1);
%%
%[text] ## Analyze Results
%[text] Extract results.
resData.Table = logsout_AirCooledDataCenterTprofile.extractTimetable;
resData.ServerT.min = resData.Table.("T.min")(end);
resData.ServerT.max = resData.Table.("T.max")(end);
resData.RoomT = resData.Table.Room(end);
disp(strcat("Server temperatures are between ",num2str(ceil(resData.ServerT.min))," K and ",... %[output:group:23ac6e6a] %[output:0aa8d818]
            num2str(ceil(resData.ServerT.max))," K.")); %[output:group:23ac6e6a] %[output:0aa8d818]
disp(strcat("Data center aisle temperature is maintained at ",num2str(ceil(resData.RoomT))," K")); %[output:303631a6]
disp(strcat("Total electrical power consumption ~ ",num2str(round(sum(diff(resData.Table.Time(2:end)).*resData.Table.E(3:end))/(resData.Table.Time(end))))," kW.")); %[output:362b29f3]

